From: ththeod <2376818+ththeod@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:43:35 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 122/138] RAM tier: resume at the previous turn's prompt-end
 tail; tail-chunk store index; fill and row-kind metrics

The partial-tail scan started at the complete hit, which stops at the newest
Mamba-aligned state (one to two blocks before the prompt end), so the previous
turn's tail checkpoint was unreachable and RAM resumes fell back to an older
aligned state (agent turns recomputed ~15K tokens). Anchor the scan at the end
of the attention prefix present in the offload store (newest block first, plus
the block before and the original block). After a partial-tail load, the tail's
chunk is now stored once it fills (it was skipped). New metrics:
kv_offload_cpu_cache_filled_chunks / total_chunks, stored_rows_{chunk,boundary,tail}.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
